Russia's war on Ukraine dominated  today's G20 Summit talks President Biden  is meeting with other world leaders in  Indonesia delegates discuss whether  Ukraine should seek a peace deal at this  time Nancy Cordis is in Bali not a bad  place to be traveling with the president  Nancy good morning I know there's a lot  of work going on  there is Gail this Summit is a gathering  of the world's 20 largest economies and  so as you might expect they have a lot  of influence in world affairs and so  Ukraine's President Vladimir zielinski  addressed this group by video and he  urged them not to ask him to compromise  with Russia at this time he compared  Ukraine's recent liberation of the city  of Carson to D-Day he said it could be a  turning point in this war and pointedly  he referred to the Gathering here as the  g19 instead of the G20 meant as a snub  to Russian President Vladimir Putin who  chose not to attend this Gathering now  in an interview U.S treasury secretary  Janet Yellen told me she believes the  Chinese who are also here are getting  closer to condemning Russia's Invasion I  also asked her about the global shortage  of diesel fuel and what it could mean  for America  do you believe that the U.S will have  enough diesel fuel to make it through  the winter  well hopefully I believe there will be  but the East Coast really faces some  shortages and low inventories so  um we're keeping a close eye in  monitoring that  she said she also hopes that diesel fuel  prices don't go up again because if they  do then prices for all kinds of goods  will likely go up as well because diesel  fuel is so heavily used in  transportation so she says that that's  something that she's going to be  watching very closely could obviously  make packages this winter around  Christmas time more expensive Nate  that's Dakota zambali thank you
 

